<main>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="page">
      <h1>Age Suitability</h1>
      <p class="page-intro">Gus is a Jellyfin client. Age appropriateness depends on the content available on the user's own Jellyfin server.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page">
    <div class="content-grid">
      <div>
        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>What Gus does</h2>
          <p>A Playa Named Gus connects users to Jellyfin servers they provide. Users access their own media libraries through the app.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>What Gus does not do</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Gus does not host, curate, sell, or distribute media.</li>
            <li>Gus does not provide unrestricted web access.</li>
            <li>Gus does not include chat, messaging, advertising, gambling, contests, loot boxes, or monetized chance mechanics.</li>
            <li>Gus does not determine the maturity rating of every user's media library.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Content access</h2>
          <p>Age appropriateness depends on the libraries, metadata, and permissions configured on the user's Jellyfin server. The server owner controls which users can access which libraries and content.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Guidance for parents and guardians</h2>
          <p>Parents and guardians should manage access through Jellyfin user permissions, Jellyfin library restrictions, and Apple Screen Time. Review the connected server's content and user settings before giving a child access to the app.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>App Review context</h2>
          <p>Because Gus can browse and play user-supplied media whose content is outside the app developer's control, the App Store age rating may reflect access to user-provided media rather than developer-hosted content.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

